# UI / views layer

React-flavoured code lives in `src/components/`. Editor surface is `NodeEditor.tsx`; per-processor UI in `flow-nodes/views/`; chrome and widgets in `flow-nodes/`. Engine is consumed via `EngineContext` — node views never import `DataflowEngine` directly.

Scene is multi-page (tabs of independent scenarios) and supports UI-only **clones** (viewer aliases of any node anywhere). Engine sees a single flat dataflow — pages and clones resolved by `sceneResolver.resolveSceneForEngine` before reaching `engine.setEdges`.

## Top-level structure

```
src/
├── theme.ts                     # MUI dark theme (Geist palette, JetBrains Mono)
├── App.tsx                      # BrowserRouter → '/' → NodeEditor
└── components/
    ├── NodeEditor.tsx           # Orchestrator (multi-page; engine sync via sceneResolver)
    ├── node-editor/             # Editor sub-components
    │   ├── constants.ts         # GRID_SIZE, snapToGrid, nextId, SLOT_COMPAT
    │   ├── menuGroups.ts        # Add Node menu
    │   ├── sceneResolver.ts     # PageState + resolveSceneForEngine + cycle check + page id minting
    │   ├── SceneContext.tsx     # Multi-page state provider
    │   ├── PublishInspector.tsx # right rail: supplier-exposure for selected node + PublishRoot summary
    │   ├── NodeEditorToolbar.tsx
    │   ├── NodeEditorTabs.tsx
    │   ├── AddNodePopover.tsx
    │   └── hooks/
    │       ├── usePipelineEngine.ts
    │       ├── useSceneHistory.ts
    │       ├── useNodeEditorShortcuts.ts
    │       ├── useEdgeColouring.ts        # clone-aware
    │       └── useDerivedSurface.ts       # memoised derivePublishedSurface(pages)
    └── flow-nodes/
        ├── nodeTypes.ts         # processor type → React component (incl. `clone`)
        ├── BaseNodeShell.tsx    # chrome + REF badge + inline rename
        ├── EditableStepEdge.tsx # custom orthogonal edge
        ├── NodePinTerminal.tsx  # bottom horizontal terminal: pinned nodes (any page)
        ├── SceneOutlineSidebar.tsx  # left rail: pages → originals; click=jumpTo, drag=create clone
        ├── categoryColors.ts
